List status,Desirability,Tier,Admission likelihood,Warnings,University,Course,Country,City,Subject rank,Overall rank,Entry requirements,Student grades,Fits grades?,English req,Backup entry route,Annual tuition,Total tuition,Est. living/yr,Duration (yrs),Approx total (MYR),Scholarship & portal,Scholarship coverage,Scholarship competitiveness,How to get the scholarship,Money to show (visa),Work rights after graduating,Recognised in Malaysia?,How to apply,Key deadline,Intake,Notes,Course URL,Info source
Longlist,81,A,Reach,Over budget,Massachusetts Institute of Technology,SB Mechanical Engineering (Course 2),USA,"Cambridge, MA",US News #1 undergrad Mechanical Eng; QS #1 Mechanical,QS ~#1 world,"Holistic, no fixed cutoff. A-Levels far exceed the academic bar; selectivity is holistic + SAT/ACT (now required). Admit rate ~4%.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet (TOEFL ~100+ / IELTS 7.0 typical) — verify Stage 4,,USD 64730,USD 258920,USD 24000,4,1668124,Need-based MIT Scholarship via CSS Profile (sfs.mit.edu). MIT is need-blind for international applicants and meets 100% of demonstrated need.,"Full demonstrated financial need, met with grants (no loans) — no merit/athletic scholarships exist; all aid is need-based.","Aid is GUARANTEED if admitted (need-blind for internationals) — the hard part is admission, not the funding. Net cost depends on family income assessed via CSS Profile.",Submit the International CSS Profile + parent financial verification alongside the Common App; no separate scholarship application.,~USD 90k/yr shown for the I-20 at sticker; drops to the aid-assessed net cost after the scholarship is set,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT extension (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs work; H-1B lottery after. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord signatory; maps to BEM Professional Engineer route. MQA recognises ABET US engineering degrees. Verify the specific programme's ABET status at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-01 (Common App Regular — provisional; EA ~Nov 2026; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"THE aid play: #1 Mech Eng in the world AND need-blind + meets-full-need for internationals. At STICKER (~RM1.67M) it busts the RM500k ceiling badly -> Over budget flag is correct; viability hinges entirely on the CSS-Profile aid assessment, which for a family that can fund RM500k may leave a real gap. SAT/ACT is REQUIRED (reinstated) and he has NO score yet -> hard action item with a deadline. All-Reach is expected for US Mech Eng; Safety comes from Japan/SG-MY later.",https://meche.mit.edu/education/undergraduate,Not verified
Longlist,81,A,Reach,Over budget,Princeton University,BSE Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering,USA,"Princeton, NJ",US News #10 undergrad Mechanical Eng,Top 1-3 national (US News),Holistic. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Admit rate ~4%.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 62400,USD 249600,USD 22000,4,1586720,Need-based Princeton aid. Need-blind for internationals; meets 100% of need with the most generous grant-only (no-loan) package in the US.,"Full demonstrated need, all grant (no loans). Princeton is often the cheapest net cost of the elites for families with need.",GUARANTEED if admitted (need-blind for internationals). Admission is the only gate.,Complete Princeton's own financial aid application + CSS Profile with the Common App; no separate scholarship form.,~USD 85k/yr shown for the I-20 at sticker; net drops sharply after Princeton's grant,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. Verify programme ABET at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-01 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"Best-funded of the elites: need-blind for internationals AND grant-only (no-loan). If any US school can land inside RM500k net for a middle-income family, it's Princeton — but only if the CSS assessment grants deep aid. Over budget at sticker (~RM1.58M). SAT/ACT required; no score yet.",https://mae.princeton.edu/undergraduate,Not verified
Finalist,78,A,Reach,Over budget,California Institute of Technology,BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Pasadena, CA",US News #6 undergrad Mechanical Eng,QS ~top 10 world,"Holistic, extremely quantitative. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Admit rate ~3%.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS/Duolingo — waived if secondary instruction was English (Sunway A-Levels qualify) but Caltech strongly recommends a score; none taken yet,,USD 68574,USD 274296,USD 30048,4,1854094,"Need-based Caltech aid via CSS Profile. Caltech meets 100% of demonstrated need for international students, but is NEED-AWARE for internationals.",Full demonstrated need met if admitted (grants).,NEED-AWARE for internationals: requesting aid can affect admission odds (unlike the need-blind set). Aid met if admitted.,Submit CSS Profile with the application; internationals must request aid up front (you cannot ask later).,~USD 90k/yr shown for the I-20 at sticker; net drops after aid,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. BS Mechanical Engineering is ABET-EAC accredited (since 2002; next review 2029-30) — recognition gate PASSES.,Common App / QuestBridge,2027-01-05 (Regular Decision; REA 2026-11-01),2027 Sept (Fall),"VERIFIED 2026-07-25 on official Caltech pages. Official 2026-27 COA USD 98,622/yr (tuition 68,574 + fees 2,655 + housing 12,711 + food 9,285 + books/personal 5,397) -> ~RM1.85M over 4 yrs (up from the ~RM1.63M snippet estimate). NEED-AWARE for internationals BUT meets 100% of demonstrated need if admitted; CSS Profile required; internationals MUST request aid at time of application or are permanently barred from applying later. SAT/ACT REQUIRED (no score yet). English test waived if instruction was English (Sunway qualifies) but strongly recommended. BS ME is ABET-EAC accredited (since 2002) -> BEM/Washington Accord gate PASSES. RD deadline 5 Jan 2027 (REA 1 Nov 2026); Fall 2027 intake matches his Sept preference. Still Over budget: RM1.85M vs RM500k ceiling, and need-aware aid is not guaranteed.",https://www.mece.caltech.edu/academics/ug,Official page
Longlist,78,A,Reach,Over budget,Cornell University,BS Mechanical Engineering (Sibley School),USA,"Ithaca, NY",US News #8 undergrad Mechanical Eng,Ivy; top 15 national,"Holistic, engineering-college admit. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Eng admit rate ~7%.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 68000,USD 272000,USD 21000,4,1673200,"Cornell need-based aid (CSS Profile). Meets 100% of demonstrated need for internationals, but is NEED-AWARE for internationals.",Full demonstrated need met if admitted (grant-based).,NEED-AWARE for internationals: requesting aid can lower admission odds. Aid met once admitted.,Submit CSS Profile with the Common App; internationals must indicate aid need at application.,~USD 89k/yr for the I-20 at sticker; net drops after aid,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. Verify programme ABET at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-02 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"Strongest Ivy Mech Eng (#8, dedicated Sibley School) — best course reputation of the Ivies here. But NEED-AWARE for internationals, so the aid request is part of the admission gamble (unlike Princeton/Harvard/Yale/Dartmouth/Brown). Over budget at sticker (~RM1.68M). SAT/ACT required; no score yet.",https://www.mae.cornell.edu/mae/programs/undergraduate-programs,Not verified
Finalist,78,A,Reach,Over budget,Johns Hopkins University,BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Baltimore, MD",US News #11 undergrad Mechanical Eng,Top 15 national (US News),"Holistic; ~5.1% admit (Class 2029, record low). A-Levels exceed the academic bar. SAT/ACT REQUIRED again (test-optional ended). TOEFL ~100+ or English-medium waiver.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL ~100+ required; English-medium A-Level waiver likely — confirm. Not taken yet.,,"USD 66,670","USD 266,680","USD 25,330 (full COA ~USD 92k/yr)",4,1616800,"JHU need-based aid; NEED-AWARE for internationals; meets 100% demonstrated need, no loans. Tuition Promise (from 2026-27): free tuition if family income <= USD 200k, $0 parent cost <= USD 100k — internationals eligible ONLY if they applied for and received aid at admission. CSS Profile (or JHU int'l aid form) + Certification of Finances.",Up to 100% of need (Tuition Promise covers tuition/fees/housing/dining under USD 100k income) — if funded.,Only ~10% of internationals receive aid; a small number of merit awards.,Request aid as a FIRST-YEAR applicant (irreversible — cannot apply in later years). File CSS Profile/int'l aid form + Certification of Finances with the Common App.,~USD 92k/yr (full COA) at sticker; drops after aid.,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,Yes — BS ME ABET-accredited (Engineering Accreditation Commission) -> Washington Accord -> BEM (Ir.) route. Confirmed on JHU catalogue/ME dept.,Common App,ED I ~2026-11-01; ED II/RD ~2027-01-02 (verify int'l date),2027 Sept (Fall),"Strong Mech Eng (#11), meets-full-need but need-aware for internationals. Slightly softer admit than the Ivies. Over budget at sticker (~RM1.62M). Confirm test policy + ABET at Stage 4. | Verified 2026-07-25 vs official JHU pages: admit ~5.1% (Class 2029); SAT/ACT required again; COA ~USD 92k/yr; need-aware for intl; Tuition Promise extends to intl only if aid granted at admission; ABET (EAC) confirmed. Dossier built (university mode).",https://me.jhu.edu/undergraduate-studies/,Official page
Longlist,76,A,Reach,Over budget,Harvard University,AB/SB Engineering Sciences (Mechanical track),USA,"Cambridge, MA",US News top-ranked engineering (Eng Sciences),QS top 5 world,Holistic. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Admit rate ~3%.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 59000,USD 236000,USD 22000,4,1522800,Harvard need-based aid (CSS Profile). Need-blind for internationals; meets 100% of need on the same basis as US students.,"Full demonstrated need, grant-based (no loans). Families under set income thresholds pay near zero.",GUARANTEED if admitted (need-blind for internationals). Admission is the gate.,Submit CSS Profile + parent financials with the Common App; no separate scholarship application.,~USD 82k/yr for the I-20 at sticker; net drops sharply after aid,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,SB Engineering Sciences is ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. The AB (non-ABET) does NOT — he must take the SB. Verify at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-01 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"Engineering at Harvard is 'Engineering Sciences' — the ABET-accredited, BEM-mappable degree is the SB, not the AB; picking the AB would break his recognition gate. Need-blind + meets-full-need for internationals. Over budget at sticker (~RM1.5M). SAT/ACT required; no score yet.",https://seas.harvard.edu/mechanical-engineering,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Reach,Over budget,Georgia Institute of Technology,BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Atlanta, GA",US News #4 undergrad Mechanical Eng,Top public; QS ~top 100 world,"Holistic + rigor-focused. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Overall admit ~16%, engineering more competitive for internationals.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 33794,USD 135176,USD 20000,4,1011327,Very limited need aid for internationals at a public. Some competitive merit scholarships (small). Budget as full sticker.,Minimal for internationals — no meets-full-need commitment.,Merit awards are few and small; do not count on aid to close the gap.,Automatic merit consideration on the application; no separate need-based route for internationals.,~USD 54k/yr shown for the I-20 (near full sticker — little aid),F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; strong Atlanta co-op/industry pipeline. H-1B lottery after.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. Verify programme ABET at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-04 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"Reputation anchor: #4 Mech Eng, elite engineering culture and co-op pipeline. But as a public it gives almost no need aid to internationals -> budget as full sticker (~RM1.01M) -> Over budget, and the scholarship lever that helps the Ivies does NOT help here. A strong name if the family could stretch, but the funding story is weak.",https://www.me.gatech.edu/academics/undergraduate,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Match,Over budget,Purdue University--Main Campus,BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"West Lafayette, IN",US News #7 undergrad Mechanical Eng,Top public engineering; QS ~top 100-150,"Holistic but less selective than the Ivies/GT. A-Levels well exceed the bar; SAT/ACT test-flexible (verify). Overall admit ~50%, engineering competitive for internationals.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 29000,USD 116000,USD 18000,4,883600,Limited need aid for internationals; some competitive merit (Trustees/Presidential) that partly offset. Budget mostly as sticker.,Partial at best for internationals — no meets-full-need commitment.,"Merit awards competitive and partial; may shave, not close, the gap.",Automatic merit consideration on the application; check international-specific awards at Stage 4.,~USD 47k/yr shown for the I-20 (cheapest of the US publics here),F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; famous co-op/industry pipeline. H-1B lottery after.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. Verify programme ABET at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-15 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"The one US Match on admissibility: #7 Mech Eng, top-tier ME reputation, but far less lottery-like than the Ivies/GT — his A* profile is genuinely strong here. Also the CHEAPEST US row (~RM884k sticker), though still Over budget and with only partial int'l aid. If he wants a realistic US admit, this is it; the gap to close is money, not grades.",https://engineering.purdue.edu/ME/Academics/Undergraduate,Not verified
