Longlist,74,B,Reach,Over budget,Brown University,ScB Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Providence, RI",Solid engineering; subject rank modest vs peers,Ivy; top 15 national,Holistic. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required (reinstated). Admit rate ~5%.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 68000,USD 272000,USD 22000,4,1692000,Brown need-based aid (CSS Profile). Need-blind for internationals from the Class of 2029; meets 100% of need.,"Full demonstrated need, grant-based (no packaged loans).",GUARANTEED if admitted (newly need-blind for internationals).,Submit CSS Profile + parent financials with the Common App; no separate scholarship application.,~USD 90k/yr for the I-20 at sticker; net drops after aid,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,ScB is ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. Verify programme ABET at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-03 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),Newly need-blind for internationals (Class of 2029) and meets-full-need; the ScB (not the AB) is the ABET degree. Open-curriculum culture. Over budget at sticker (~RM1.69M). SAT/ACT required; no score yet.,https://engineering.brown.edu/academics/undergraduate,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Reach,Over budget,Dartmouth College,AB Engineering Sciences / BE Mechanical (ABET),USA,"Hanover, NH","Thayer School — well-regarded, subject rank modest",Ivy; top 15 national,Holistic. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Admit rate ~6%.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 66000,USD 264000,USD 22000,4,1654400,Dartmouth need-based aid (CSS Profile). Universal need-blind policy now includes all international citizens (Class of 2026+); meets 100% of need.,"Full demonstrated need, grant-based (no loans).","GUARANTEED if admitted — Dartmouth extended need-blind to internationals, so requesting aid no longer hurts odds.",Submit CSS Profile + parent financials with the Common App; no separate scholarship application.,~USD 88k/yr for the I-20 at sticker; net drops after aid,F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; H-1B lottery after.,The ABET-accredited degree is the BE (a 4th/5th-year add-on to the AB); the standalone 4-year AB is NOT ABET. For the BEM/Washington-Accord gate he must complete the BE. Verify at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-01-03 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"Recently need-blind for internationals (confirmed on the Thayer + admissions pages) and meets-full-need. RECOGNITION NUANCE: only the BE is ABET/BEM-mappable, not the 4-year AB — the AB alone would fail his engineering gate. Over budget at sticker (~RM1.65M). SAT/ACT required; no score yet.",https://engineering.dartmouth.edu/academics/undergraduate,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Reach,Over budget,University of Michigan--Ann Arbor,BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Ann Arbor, MI",US News #4 undergrad Mechanical Eng,Top public; QS ~top 25 world,"Holistic. A-Levels exceed the bar; SAT/ACT required. Overall admit ~18%, engineering competitive for internationals.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Exceeds academic bar,TOEFL/IELTS required; no test taken yet — verify Stage 4,,USD 60000,USD 240000,USD 20000,4,1504000,Very limited need aid for internationals at a public. Small competitive merit awards only. Budget as full sticker.,Minimal for internationals — no meets-full-need commitment.,Merit awards few and small; do not count on aid.,Automatic merit consideration on the application; no need-based route for internationals.,~USD 80k/yr shown for the I-20 (near full sticker),F-1 -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT (Mech Eng is STEM) = up to 3 yrs; strong auto/industry pipeline. H-1B lottery after.,ABET-accredited -> Washington Accord; maps to BEM route. Verify programme ABET at Stage 4.,Common App,2027-02-01 (Regular — provisional; verify Stage 4),2027 Sept (Fall),"Reputation anchor: #4 Mech Eng, huge automotive/industry pipeline. Most expensive public here for internationals (~RM1.5M sticker) with negligible int'l need aid -> Over budget with no funding lever. Kept for the name; the cost story is worse than Georgia Tech/Purdue.",https://me.engin.umich.edu/academics/undergraduate/,Not verified
Finalist,84,A,Match,,National University of Singapore,Bachelor of Engineering (Mechanical Engineering),Singapore,Singapore,QS Mechanical/Aero/Manufacturing ~top 10 world; NUS overall QS top 10,QS ~#8 world,Common 'Engineering' admissions: pass in H2 Mathematics (or Further Maths); Physics not mandatory (bridging course if missing). IGP is for Singapore-Cambridge A-Levels; international places are capped/competitive.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,IELTS/TOEFL may be required unless English-medium instruction is accepted as a waiver; he took A-Levels in English at Sunway. Verify per-applicant at Stage 4.,"Admitted to the common Engineering programme, then declare the Mechanical Engineering major — no internal quota between engineering majors.",SGD 18050,SGD 72200,SGD 18000,4,476000,"ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship (NUS) — considered on the admission application for outstanding ASEAN freshmen; plus the MOE Tuition Grant (subsidised fee, above).","ASEAN UG: 100% of subsidised (post-Tuition-Grant) tuition + S$5,800/yr living allowance + S$1,750 one-time computer allowance + settling-in allowance.","Competitive, interview-selected; awarded to a limited number of top ASEAN applicants.",Indicate/apply alongside the NUS admission application; shortlisted candidates are interviewed. Verify exact form vs auto-consideration at Stage 4.,Student's Pass financial requirement shown at visa stage (verify amount Stage 4).,"No post-study-work visa. Student's Pass lapses ~30 days after graduation; staying needs an Employment Pass (min salary S$6,000/mo general from 1 Jan 2027, + COMPASS). The MOE Tuition Grant carries a 3-year bond working for a Singapore-registered company — a guaranteed 3 years of local work, though a long-term stay still runs through the EP bar. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.","BEng (ME) is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Board (EAB) of Singapore, a Washington Accord signatory -> maps to the BEM Professional Engineer route back home. MQA recognises Washington-Accord degrees. Verify the specific programme's current accreditation at Stage 4.",NUS Office of Admissions (nus.edu.sg/oam) — direct international application,~2027-02 (AY2027/28 intl window ~Dec 2026-Feb 2027; confirm exact dates),2027 Aug (maps to his Sept 2027 preference; one intake/year),"VERIFIED 2026-07-25 vs official NUS pages. Fee confirmed on the NUS Registrar UG fee PDF (AY2026/27 new intake): Design & Engineering, International WITH MOE Tuition Grant, ASEAN tier = S$18,050/yr (S$39,700/yr WITHOUT the grant). 4-yr total ~S$144k (tuition ~S$72k + living ~S$72k) ~ RM476k, just inside RM500k but tight and FX/living-cost sensitive. THE catch: the affordable fee requires the MOE Tuition Grant, which binds 3 years' work in Singapore (break-bond ~S$80-120k) — clashes with intent_to_migrate=Unsure. Entry: predicted A*A*A*A* sits at/above NUS Engineering IGP 90th pct (band BCC/B to AAA/A) -> comfortable Match. B.Eng(ME) EAB-accredited -> Washington Accord -> BEM route (a recognition strength vs the US rows). Aug 2027 intake (not Sept). Dossier built (course mode) 2026-07-25.",https://cde.nus.edu.sg/me/undergraduate/beng-me/overview/,Official page
Shortlist,84,A,Match,,Nanyang Technological University,Bachelor of Engineering (Mechanical Engineering),Singapore,Singapore,"#1 in Asia and #4 in the world for Mechanical, Aeronautical & Manufacturing (QS 2025 by subject)",QS ~#15 world,H2 pass in Mathematics AND H2 pass in Physics/Chemistry/Biology/Computing (Singapore-Cambridge A-Level). IGP for Singapore-Cambridge A-Levels; international places capped/competitive.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,IELTS 6.0+ / TOEFL 90+ typically; may be waived for English-medium instruction. Verify per-applicant at Stage 4.,"Accelerated Bachelor's (3.5 yr) if strong in Year 1 Sem 1 — would cut a year of cost. Second-major options (Business, Data Analytics, Sustainability) available.",SGD 19000,SGD 76000,SGD 15000,4,476000,"ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship (NTU) — offered to outstanding ASEAN freshmen; plus the MOE Tuition Grant (subsidised fee, above).","ASEAN UG: full coverage of subsidised (post-Tuition-Grant) tuition + S$5,800/yr living allowance + International Student allowance + computer allowance.","Competitive, leadership + academic + co-curricular selection; interview.",Considered via the NTU admission application for ASEAN citizens (largely auto-considered — that structure is worth more than a separately-won award). Verify exact process at Stage 4.,Student's Pass financial requirement shown at visa stage (verify amount Stage 4).,"No post-study-work visa. Student's Pass lapses at graduation; staying needs an Employment Pass (min salary S$6,000/mo general from 1 Jan 2027 + COMPASS). The MOE Tuition Grant 3-year bond guarantees 3 years of Singapore work; long-term stay runs through the EP bar. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.","BEng (Mechanical Engineering) is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Board of the Institution of Engineers, Singapore (IES) -> Washington Accord -> maps to the BEM Professional Engineer route. Verify current accreditation at Stage 4.",NTU Office of Admissions — direct international application,,2027 Aug (maps to his Sept 2027 preference; one intake/year),"The strongest Singapore row on subject reputation — #4 in the WORLD for the mechanical subject cluster, and the same Washington-Accord/BEM recognition as NUS. Fee tier = International WITH Tuition Grant (ASEAN); MOE sets subsidised tiers so NTU's figure should match NUS's to the dollar — ~S$19k/yr provisional pending the AY2026-27 fee PDF at Stage 4. Total ~RM476k, just inside RM500k. Accelerated 3.5-yr option could drop it further.",https://www.ntu.edu.sg/spms/admissions/undergrad/detail/bachelor-of-engineering-in-mechanical-engineering,Not verified
Longlist,76,A,Match,,Singapore University of Technology and Design,Bachelor of Engineering (Engineering Product Development) — Mechanical Engineering track,Singapore,Singapore,No standalone global subject rank; SUTD is design/innovation-focused (MIT-collaboration heritage),Younger university; modest overall global rank,Holistic admissions (grades + portfolio/aptitude). A-Level Maths + a science expected. International places competitive.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,IELTS/TOEFL typically required unless English-medium waiver applies. Verify Stage 4.,EPD is a broad-based engineering degree; the Mechanical Engineering track is chosen within it.,SGD 19000,SGD 76000,SGD 15000,4,476000,"SUTD scholarships + MOE Tuition Grant (subsidised fee, above). NOT eligible for the ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship (that is NUS/NTU/SMU only).",MOE Tuition Grant subsidy; SUTD-specific awards vary.,Varies by award.,Apply via SUTD admissions/scholarships. Verify Stage 4.,Student's Pass financial requirement (verify Stage 4).,"Same as other SG publics: no PSW visa; Employment Pass (S$6,000/mo, 2027) for long-term stay; MOE Tuition Grant 3-year bond guarantees 3 years local work. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.","EPD is EAB-accredited (Washington Accord) -> BEM route -- BUT confirm the Mechanical Engineering TRACK carries the accreditation and maps to BEM, since EPD is a broad product-development degree, not a titled 'Mechanical Engineering' degree. Flag for Stage 4.",SUTD Admissions — direct international application,,2027 (SUTD's academic year; verify intake month vs his Sept preference at Stage 4),"Mechanical Engineering here is a TRACK inside the Engineering Product Development degree, not a standalone Mech-Eng programme -- score course_match for what it actually is (broad product design + a mech specialisation). SUTD's project/design-build pedagogy is the strongest experiential fit of the SG set. Softer, holistic entry than NUS/NTU -> a genuine Match. Recognition (does the EPD/mech track map to BEM?) is the key Stage-4 check.",https://www.sutd.edu.sg/epd/education/undergraduate/specialisation-tracks/mechanical-engineering/,Not verified
Longlist,76,A,Safety,,Singapore Institute of Technology,Bachelor of Engineering with Honours in Mechanical Engineering,Singapore,Singapore,Applied/industry-focused; no global subject ranking,Applied university; not globally ranked,Applied-entry (grades + suitability). Three-year direct-honours programme. International intake is limited (SIT primarily serves Singaporeans/PRs).,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,IELTS/TOEFL as required; verify Stage 4.,"Related SIT option: BEng (Hons) Mechanical Design & Manufacturing Engineering (MDME), a 3-yr direct-honours joint-degree — an alternative if pure Mech Eng is full.",SGD 18000,SGD 54000,SGD 15000,3,346500,MOE Tuition Grant (subsidised fee). NOT eligible for the ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship. SIT-specific awards limited for internationals.,"MOE Tuition Grant subsidy only, in practice.",Limited international scholarship availability.,Apply via SIT admissions. Verify Stage 4.,Student's Pass financial requirement (verify Stage 4).,"Same SG regime: no PSW visa; EP (S$6,000/mo, 2027) for long-term; MOE Tuition Grant 3-year bond. SIT's work-integrated model (Integrated Work Study Programme) gives strong local industry ties. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.",SIT engineering degrees are EAB-accredited (Washington Accord) -> BEM route -- verify the specific Mechanical Engineering programme's accreditation at Stage 4.,SIT Admissions — direct international application,,2027 (verify intake month vs his Sept preference at Stage 4),"The cheapest Singapore row -- driven by the 3-YEAR duration (vs 4 at NUS/NTU/SUTD), not a lower annual fee -- ~RM330-350k, comfortably inside budget, and applied/work-integrated (strong experiential). BUT two real caveats for Stage 4: (1) SIT's international undergraduate intake is limited, so admission is not a clean Safety despite his grades clearing the bar; (2) confirm the programme is EAB/Washington-Accord accredited for his BEM gate. On grades alone it is his softest Singapore entry.",https://www.singaporetech.edu.sg/undergraduate-programmes/mechanical-engineering,Not verified
Longlist,79,A,Match,,"Institute of Science Tokyo (Science Tokyo, former Tokyo Tech)",Global Scientists and Engineers Program (GSEP) — B.Eng. in Transdisciplinary Science and Engineering,Japan,Tokyo,Former Tokyo Institute of Technology — Japan's leading science & engineering institute; top-tier engineering reputation,"QS ~#80-120 world (Science Tokyo, provisional post-merger)","Selective: preliminary document screening then a written exam (high-school maths, physics, chemistry) + interview. Tiny cohort — 8 MEXT + 10 privately funded = 18 seats/year. A-Level/IB/SAT are optional reference materials.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,"TOEFL iBT / IELTS Academic / TOEIC L&R required (no minimum score), taken within 2 yrs. Malaysians are NOT exempt (exemption only for AU/CA/IE/NZ/UK/US nationals) despite English-medium schooling -> he MUST sit a test. None taken yet.","None for mechanical specifically — GSEP is transdisciplinary; specialisation is via course choice within the Dept of Transdisciplinary Science & Engineering, not a titled mech-eng track.",JPY 635400,JPY 2823600,JPY 1200000,4,236332,"MEXT (GSEP university-recommendation, priority) — und.gsep@adm.isct.ac.jp; JASSO Honors Scholarship as fallback","MEXT (8 seats): no enrollment fee or tuition + 120,000 yen/month for 4 years + airfare. JASSO fallback: 48,000 yen/month (fees still payable).",Only 8 MEXT seats among the 18-student cohort -> highly competitive; annual GPA >= 2.3 review to keep it.,Top 8 who pass the GSEP examination are recommended for MEXT — considered through the same admission process.,"Application fee JPY 17,000; student-visa financial proof at visa stage for self-funded applicants.","Tokyo, top engineering institute -> strong domestic and multinational hiring; student visa -> Engineer/Specialist work visa or job-hunting extension. Japanese-language ability shapes outcomes. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.",MQA recognises the degree. BEM route needs JABEE/Washington-Accord accreditation — a TRANSDISCIPLINARY B.Eng. (not a titled Mechanical Engineering degree) makes the BEM mapping especially uncertain; verify carefully at Stage 4.,The Admissions Office (TAO / admissions-office.net) online application,"2026-08-21 (application period Aug 12-21, 2026; results Nov 13, 2026; enrollment Mar 2027 for April 2027 start)",2027 Apr (April enrollment ONLY — does not match his Sept 2027 preference; admission process also changes from AY2028),"Highest academic prestige of the Japan set (former Tokyo Tech), fully English B.Eng., ~RM236k total. But three real caveats: (1) course_match is soft — it's a TRANSDISCIPLINARY engineering degree, not titled Mechanical Engineering (the SUTD-EPD situation), which also weakens the BEM mapping; (2) April-only intake mismatches his Sept preference and the application closed-window is Aug 2026 (very soon); (3) admission is a written maths/physics/chemistry exam + interview into an 18-seat cohort -> competitive despite his strong grades, so scored Match not Safety. He must also sit TOEFL/IELTS (no Malaysian exemption).",https://admissions.isct.ac.jp/en/013/undergraduate/programs/gsep,Not verified
Longlist,74,B,Safety,,Nagoya University,"B.Eng. in Automotive Engineering (Mechanical Engineering Program, G30)",Japan,Nagoya,"Strong mechanical/automotive engineering (RU11 national; heart of Japan's automotive belt, Toyota ecosystem)",QS ~#150 world (provisional),"Recommended A-Level A*AA and above (or SAT Math ~760+, IB 40/42 with Math AA HL / Physics HL 6-7). Fully English-taught G30; international seats are limited/competitive.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,English-taught G30; English proficiency evidence expected. He took A-Levels in English (Sunway). No TOEFL/IELTS taken yet — verify per-applicant requirement at Stage 4.,"Sister track: Automotive Engineering - Electrical, Electronic & Information Engineering (same program, EEIE track) if the mechanical track is full.",JPY 535800,JPY 2425200,JPY 950000,4,192981,MEXT (university-recommended) + Nagoya G30 tuition/financial support — see admissions.g30.nagoya-u.ac.jp/studentlife/scholarships/,MEXT (if recommended): full tuition + enrollment-fee exemption + monthly stipend + airfare. Nagoya also has partial tuition-support schemes.,"MEXT university-recommendation is competitive and limited; treat as upside, not a given.",Considered via the G30 admission application for the strongest applicants; verify exact MEXT-recommendation mechanism at Stage 4.,Student visa (Certificate of Eligibility) financial proof at visa stage — verify amount Stage 4.,"Graduates switch from student visa to a work visa (Engineer/Specialist in Humanities) or the ~1-yr Designated Activities job-hunting extension. Strong automotive/manufacturing pipeline (Toyota, Mitsubishi Fuso, Woven by Toyota in alumni list), but actual employability is shaped by Japanese-language ability. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.",MQA recognises Japanese national-university degrees for study/employment. BEM Professional Engineer route needs Washington Accord (JABEE) accreditation of THIS programme — JABEE accreditation of English-taught G30 programmes is often absent and is UNVERIFIED here; a real risk for his BEM gate. Verify JABEE status at Stage 4.,Nagoya University G30 online application (admissions.g30.nagoya-u.ac.jp),"Two rounds: Round 1 Nov-Dec 2026, Round 2 Jan 2027 (verify exact dates Stage 4)",2027 (G30 undergrad — verify April vs autumn/October intake vs his Sept preference at Stage 4),"The cleanest EMI mechanical fit in Japan: the only Japanese university specialising in automotive engineering taught fully in English, degree B.Eng. with a core mechanical curriculum (thermodynamics, mechanics of materials, fluid mechanics, vibration, control) plus automotive specialisation. Published A-Level bar A*AA which his A*A*A*A* clearly clears -> Safety on grades, though G30 international seats are capped (a real access caveat, not a grades issue). National-uni fees put the ~4-yr total near RM193k, deep inside RM500k. Two big Stage-4 checks: (1) JABEE/Washington-Accord accreditation for his BEM gate (likely the weak point of the Japan option), (2) intake month vs his Sept preference.",https://admissions.g30.nagoya-u.ac.jp/undergraduate/automotive/,Not verified
Longlist,74,B,Match,,Kyushu University,International Undergraduate Program (Engineering) — Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering,Japan,Fukuoka,RU11 national research university; dedicated Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering programme,QS ~#150-170 world (provisional),Four-year English-taught bachelor (all classes in English except Japanese-language classes). Minimum standardized-test-score requirements apply (see the 2027 Application Instructions PDF). International undergrad admission is competitive.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,Standardized English/test-score minimums per the application instructions; verify exact bar at Stage 4. No TOEFL/IELTS taken yet.,"No transfer/credit system — must start from year 1. Sister programmes in the same intake: Electrical Eng & Computer Science, Applied Chemistry, Civil Eng.",JPY 535800,JPY 2425200,JPY 900000,4,186781,MEXT (Kyushu university-recommendation) — nyu-inquiry@jimu.kyushu-u.ac.jp,"MEXT (if recommended): 117,000 yen/month for 4 years + full enrollment-fee AND tuition exemption (4 years) + round-trip airfare.","A few of the strongest successful applicants are individually contacted and recommended to MEXT — competitive, not guaranteed.",No separate form: Kyushu selects top admitted applicants and recommends them to MEXT after admission.,Student visa financial proof at visa stage — verify amount Stage 4.,Student visa -> work visa (Engineer/Specialist in Humanities) or ~1-yr job-hunting extension. Employability shaped by Japanese-language ability; Fukuoka is less industry-dense than Nagoya/Tokyo. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,"MQA recognises Japanese national-university degrees. BEM route needs Washington Accord (JABEE) accreditation of this specific English-taught programme — UNVERIFIED and often absent for EMI programmes; a real Stage-4 gate, not an assumption.",Kyushu University online application (guide.52school.com/net-kyushu-u) + posted documents,"2026-12-11 (online application window Dec 7-11, 2026 for Oct 2027 intake; posted documents follow)",2027 Oct (October 2027 enrollment — maps cleanly to his Sept 2027 preference),"A titled Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering degree (cleaner course_match than Nagoya's automotive-branded one), 4-yr English, October 2027 intake that maps well to his Sept preference. STRONGEST scholarship story of the Japan set: the university-recommended MEXT package (117k/mo + full tuition & enrollment exemption + airfare) is a genuine full-ride, actively offered to top admits. Application window is extremely tight (Dec 7-11 2026 online) with posted documents and standardized-test minimums -> plan the SAT/test calendar around it. ~RM187k total. Same JABEE/BEM recognition caveat as all Japan rows — the key Stage-4 check.",https://www.kyushu-u.ac.jp/en/admission/faculty/foreign/foreign10/,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Match,,Waseda University,B.Eng. in Mechanical Engineering (School of Creative Science and Engineering — English-based Undergraduate Program),Japan,Tokyo,Top private university; strong employer recognition in Japan and among Malaysian employers; Mechanical Engineering major within Creative Science & Engineering,QS ~#150-200 world (provisional),English-based degree program admission (document/AO-style screening of academic record + English + motivation). Selective but not exam-gated like GSEP.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,English-medium program; English proficiency evidence expected. Verify exact test/bar at Stage 4. No TOEFL/IELTS taken yet.,Mechanical Engineering (ME) is a named major inside the School of Creative Science & Engineering; the SHIP fieldwork course lets students confirm the major before specialising.,JPY 1760000,JPY 7240000,JPY 1200000,4,373240,Waseda scholarships for privately-financed international students + JASSO Honors Scholarship,Partial tuition-reduction awards; JASSO monthly stipend. No meets-full-need model.,Competitive; many awards assessed after enrollment on academic performance.,Via Waseda admission/scholarship application; verify auto-consideration vs separate form at Stage 4.,Student-visa financial proof at visa stage — verify amount Stage 4.,Tokyo + Japan's largest international-student body and a huge alumni/employer network -> strong Japan employability; student visa -> work visa or job-hunting extension. Japanese-language ability still matters. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,MQA recognises the degree. BEM route needs JABEE/Washington-Accord accreditation of this English-based Mechanical Engineering programme — UNVERIFIED (JABEE accreditation is uncommon for EMI programmes at private universities); a real Stage-4 gate.,Waseda University International Admissions (English-based Undergraduate Program),Verify Stage 4 (English-based program schedule; note the ASE September-intake AO route was discontinued from 2023),"2027 (English-based program — confirm the Creative Science & Engineering / Mechanical intake month; ASE's Sept enrollment was discontinued, so don't assume Sept here)","The private-university option: a titled Mechanical Engineering B.Eng. taught fully in English at Japan's most internationally-oriented private university, with the strongest name recognition among the Japan set for a Malaysian employer. Cost is the trade-off — ~JPY 1.76M/yr private tuition (PROVISIONAL) puts the total near RM373k: still inside the RM500k ceiling but ~2x the national-uni rows and with weaker scholarships (partial, not full-ride). Intake month and JABEE/BEM accreditation are the key Stage-4 checks; fees need confirming against Waseda's official schedule.",https://www.waseda.jp/fsci/en/about/education/english-based/,Not verified
Longlist,65,B,Match,,Tohoku University,"Gateway College (interdisciplinary English-taught undergraduate program, 2027-)",Japan,Sendai,RU11 national research university; historically strong engineering (its dedicated IMAC-U Mechanical & Aerospace English course is now closed to new undergrads),QS ~#100-150 world (provisional),Comprehensive selection; separate April and October intakes with different requirements. Strong academic record + English proficiency expected. Brand-new program (first intake 2027) so selectivity is not yet established.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,English-taught; proficiency evidence expected. Verify exact bar at Stage 4. No TOEFL/IELTS taken yet.,Specialisation is chosen AFTER enrollment — a mechanical/aerospace path is not guaranteed and must be confirmed; the old dedicated IMAC-U mechanical route ended its last undergrad intake in 2026.,JPY 535800,JPY 2425200,JPY 850000,4,180581,MEXT routes typical of national universities; verify Gateway College-specific scholarships at Stage 4,MEXT (if recommended): tuition/enrollment exemption + stipend + airfare. Program-specific awards TBC.,Competitive; details for the new program not yet published.,Verify at Stage 4 once Gateway College admissions details are finalised.,Student-visa financial proof at visa stage — verify amount Stage 4.,Student visa -> work visa or job-hunting extension; Japanese-language ability shapes outcomes. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,"MQA recognises Japanese national-university degrees. BEM route needs JABEE/Washington-Accord accreditation — for an INTERDISCIPLINARY degree where specialisation is chosen after enrollment, whether a mechanical/Washington-Accord-accredited pathway exists is unknown; a heavy Stage-4 check.",Tohoku University undergraduate admissions (Gateway College),Separate April and October 2027 intakes — verify exact dates at Stage 4,2027 Apr and Oct (Gateway College runs both; October could map to his Sept preference),"IMPORTANT FINDING: Tohoku's dedicated English-taught Mechanical & Aerospace course (IMAC-U, under the FGL program) has CLOSED to new undergraduate admissions (last intake 2026). For 2027 it is replaced by Gateway College, a broad INTERDISCIPLINARY English program where you pick a specialisation after enrollment. So Tohoku is no longer a clean mechanical route: course_match is low (2) because a titled mechanical/aerospace path isn't guaranteed, and the BEM/JABEE mapping is even more uncertain. Kept on the longlist as a cheap national-uni EMI option (~RM181k, Oct intake maps to Sept) but flagged as speculative pending Stage-4 confirmation that mechanical specialisation + accreditation actually exist within Gateway College.",https://www.insc.tohoku.ac.jp/english/degree/undergraduate-english/,Not verified
Longlist,88,A,Safety,,Universiti Teknologi PETRONAS (UTP),Bachelor of Mechanical Engineering with Honours,Malaysia,"Seri Iskandar, Perak",Top private engineering uni; strong graduate-employability outcomes (Petronas ecosystem),QS ~#300-350 world,Foundation/A-Level/STPM with credits in Maths+Physics. His A*A*A*A* is well above.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",Yes,English-medium; A-Levels in English generally accepted (IELTS/MUET may be requested). Verify Stage 4.,UTP Foundation in Engineering if needed; direct entry is a Safety on his grades.,MYR 26125,MYR 104500,MYR 12000,4,152500,PETRONAS Education Sponsorship Programme / Yayasan UTP merit scholarships — genuinely strong for top A-Level students.,,,,n/a (Malaysian citizen),Malaysian citizen — no visa barrier; one of the strongest graduate-employability pipelines in Malaysia (Petronas + oil/gas + engineering). intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,"Bachelor of ENGINEERING => EAC-accredited, BEM Professional Engineer route, Washington Accord (his target). Confirm the programme's EAC status at Stage 4.",UTP direct application,,2027 (Jan / May / Sept intakes; the Sept intake maps to his preference — verify),"The employability play of the Malaysian set: Petronas-owned, industry-integrated, strong hands-on/internship culture and a genuine sponsorship route his grades make him competitive for. LOCAL total ~RM104,500 (confirmed on UTP's own Local tuition-fees page) — well inside budget. Seri Iskandar, Perak (farther from home).",https://www.utp.edu.my/Pages/Admission/Undergraduate/Bachelor-of-Mechanical-Engineering-with-Honours.aspx,Not verified
