Shortlist,78,A,Reach,Over budget,Stanford University,BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Stanford, California",QS Mechanical ~#2-5 world; Stanford overall QS top-5,QS ~#3-6 world,"Highly selective, holistic (no fixed grade cutoff); rigorous STEM record expected. His A*A*A*A* is academically strong but far from a guarantee — single-digit admit rate.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",No,TOEFL/IELTS; waiver likely (English-medium A-Levels),,USD 67731,USD 270924,USD 28000,4,1799743,Need-based aid only (no merit/athletic-free-ride for most); meets 100% of demonstrated need for ALL admitted students incl. internationals. BUT admission is need-AWARE for internationals — requesting aid affects the decision. CSS Profile required.,,,,~USD 96k/yr shown for I-20 / F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12mo + 24mo STEM extension (~3 yrs total); very strong Silicon Valley / US engineering outcomes. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,"US ABET-accredited ME; USA is a Washington Accord signatory, so the degree is recognised in Malaysia and supports the BEM Professional Engineer route (confirm ABET status of the specific programme at Stage 4).",Common App / Coalition,2027-01-05 (Regular Decision; REA ~2026-11-01),2027 Sept,"Elite ME; academically a superb match but a hard Reach (single-digit admit). Over budget: full COA ~USD 96k/yr, ~RM1.8M total, well above the RM500k ceiling. Need-aware for internationals means aid is not guaranteed. Snippet-level only — verify fees/aid/deadline at Stage 4.",https://me.stanford.edu/academics-admissions/undergraduate-program,Not verified
Shortlist,75,A,Reach,Over budget,University of Pennsylvania,BSE Mechanical Engineering & Applied Mechanics (MEAM),USA,"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania",QS Mechanical ~#30-50 world; Penn SEAS solid but ME is not Penn's flagship strength,QS ~#10-15 world (Ivy League),"Ivy-selective, holistic; strong STEM record expected. His A*A*A*A* is competitive but admission is a Reach.","A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",No,TOEFL/IELTS; waiver likely (English-medium A-Levels),,USD 65670,USD 295912,USD 24000,4,1841986,"Need-based, all-grant (no loans); meets 100% of demonstrated need INCLUDING internationals. Quaker Commitment = full tuition for families under ~USD 200k (and free education under ~USD 75k). Admission is need-aware for internationals. CSS Profile required.",,,,~USD 95k/yr (COA ~USD 94.6k) shown for I-20 / F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12mo + 24mo STEM extension (~3 yrs total); strong Ivy engineering outcomes (Philadelphia / NE corridor). intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,"US ABET-accredited ME (MEAM); USA is a Washington Accord signatory, so the degree is recognised in Malaysia and supports the BEM Professional Engineer route (confirm ABET status at Stage 4).",Common App / Coalition / QuestBridge,2027-01-05 (Regular Decision; ED ~2026-11-01),2027 Sept,Ivy with genuinely strong international aid (meets full need incl. internationals) — the best aid picture of the three IF the family qualifies. Over budget at sticker (~RM1.85M total) but need-based grants could cut that sharply. ME is a notch below Stanford/Berkeley in subject reputation. Reach. Verify fees/aid/deadline at Stage 4.,https://www.me.upenn.edu/academics/undergraduate/,Not verified
Shortlist,72,B,Reach,Over budget,"University of California, Berkeley",BS Mechanical Engineering,USA,"Berkeley, California",QS Mechanical ~#3-6 world (top public); Berkeley College of Engineering elite,QS ~#10-15 world,College of Engineering direct admit is extremely selective for international applicants (well below the general Berkeley admit rate). Strong STEM record expected; his A*A*A*A* is competitive but engineering international admission is a Reach.,"A*A*A*A* predicted (Maths, Physics, Chem, Further Maths)",No,TOEFL/IELTS; waiver likely (English-medium A-Levels),,USD 48726,USD 194904,USD 26000,4,1404849,"CRITICAL: international undergraduates are INELIGIBLE for federal/state/institutional need-based aid at UC Berkeley. Only small, highly competitive merit awards (~USD 1k-5k/yr, e.g. Regents'/Chancellor's, auto-considered). Effectively full self-funding — the weakest aid picture of the three US adds.",,,,~USD 75k/yr (nonresident COA) shown for I-20 / F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12mo + 24mo STEM extension (~3 yrs total); very strong Bay Area / US engineering outcomes. intent_to_migrate = Unsure.,"US ABET-accredited ME; USA is a Washington Accord signatory, so the degree is recognised in Malaysia and supports the BEM Professional Engineer route (confirm ABET status at Stage 4).",UC Application (NOT Common App),2026-11-30 (UC application filing period 1 Oct - 30 Nov 2026),2027 Fall,"Top public ME, world-class. Cheaper than the private US options (nonresident public, ~RM1.4M total) but STILL over the RM500k budget, AND internationals get essentially no need-based aid — so out-of-pocket is high. Uses the separate UC Application with an EARLIER deadline (30 Nov 2026) — flag on the calendar. Reach for international engineering. Verify at Stage 4.",https://me.berkeley.edu/undergraduate/,Not verified
